From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5next: MoE route v2 (fused top-k + alignment)

VLLM_GLM5_ROUTE_V2 (default 0 = unchanged), VLLM_GLM5_ROUTE_V2_GEMV
(gate | tc, default gate). One launch does grouped top-8 and the block-8
alignment and hands the alignment to the compiled Marlin decode; in tc mode
it also does the gate GEMV. Gate mode is bitwise equal to the existing
router. Any unsupported layer or a missed handoff falls back to the
deterministic alignment or upstream.

